---
import PostLayout from "../layouts/PostLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import me from "../assets/me.jpg";
---

<PostLayout
	title="About Me"
	description="A little bit about myself."
	metadata={false}
>
	<p>If you ended up here, you probably have a few questions about who I am.</p>

	<h2>TL;DR</h2>

	<p>
		I'm Diogo Correia, born in 1996 in Portugal. Started my professional <a
			href="/resume">career</a
		> as a Software Engineer in 2021. On this website, you'll find technical posts,
		music content, and my thoughts on a variety of topics.
	</p>

	<figure>
		<Image
			src={me}
			alt="Me a few days after moving to Turin in 2018"
			loading="lazy"
		/>
		<figcaption>
			Me a few days after moving to <a href="https://duckduckgo.com/?q=turin"
				>Turin</a
			> in 2018.
		</figcaption>
	</figure>

	<h2>Work</h2>

	<p>
		I work as a software engineer. You can learn more about my professional
		experience on my <a href="/resume">resumé</a>.
	</p>

	<p>
		I'm a generalist programmer. From putting <a href="https://webassembly.org/"
			>WebAssembly</a
		> in microcontrollers, working on neuroscience browser applications, writing a
		Bluetooth Low Energy firewall, to deploying policy engines to Kubernetes, I've
		loved working through it all.
	</p>

	<p>
		I've been a bit self-conscious about this, but I'm starting to feel
		comfortable with it. The fallacy is that a generalist is not a master of
		anything. I believe that with great commitment, being a generalist is being
		fluent on many things. It sharpens your understanding on what is possible
		and how it can be done.
	</p>

	<h2>Technical Interests</h2>

	<p>
		I ♥ <a href="https://nixos.org/">Nix &amp; NixOS</a>. I'm a <a
			href="https://go.dev/">Go</a
		> enthusiast and <a href="https://www.cncf.io/">Cloud Native</a> advocate. A passionate
		open source partisan who believes in sustainable open software development.
	</p>

	<h2>When Not Coding</h2>

	<p>
		Music is my forever loving side passion. I plan on hoarding music gear in
		direct proportion to how much space and money I can save.
	</p>
</PostLayout>
